# APIs (REST, GraphQL, gRPC)

## Contract

- The schema (OpenAPI, GraphQL SDL, `.proto`) is the source of truth. Code and docs derive from it, or CI checks them against it.
- Version the API (path or header). Inside one version, changes are additive only; deprecate with a date and a `Sunset` header.

## Behavior

- One error envelope for every failure: code, message, details, request id. Use real status codes; never a `200` with an error body.
- Validate input at the edge. Every list endpoint paginates. Unsafe retries (charges, creates) take an idempotency key.
- Authentication and authorization are on by default; public routes are an explicit allowlist. Rate-limit by caller.

## Tests

- Contract tests against the schema, plus one happy path and one failure path per endpoint.
